<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $117.1 mln Dec 17.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $117.1 mln Dec 17.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $117.1 million surplus on December 17 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 17</p>
<p>Exports: $187.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $163.5 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $480 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $387.1 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $117.1 million</p>
<p>DECEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.399 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.375 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.267 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.154 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.137 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418</p>
